📋 Real-World Operational Scenario
• The Business Challenge: Your global corporate web application experiences highly variable traffic spikes across different time zones. The network security team requires that no application server have a public internet IP address to prevent direct targeting, while budgeting and uptime mandates require self-healing clusters that remain active across multiple geographic regions simultaneously.
• The Technical Resolution: Activated a Global HTTP Health Check framework to monitor internal application stability every 5 seconds. Provisioned zero-external-IP instance templates running automated Apache web server bootstrap metadata configurations. Initialized multi-zone Managed Instance Groups (MIGs) across both us-central1 and us-east4 to guarantee continuous high availability and automated regional failover perimeters.

# 1. Establish project environment target context safely
export MY_PROJ="project-c1a05de0-ba4b-4764-93a"

# 2. Generate the global HTTP health check probe template mapping
gcloud compute health-checks create http regional-http-health-check --port=80 --request-path="/" --check-interval=5s --timeout=5s --healthy-threshold=2 --unhealthy-threshold=3 --project=$MY_PROJ

# 3. Provision the zero-external-IP instance template for the Primary Region (US Central)
gcloud compute instance-templates create central-app-template --network=enterprise-global-vpc --subnet=prod-central-app-subnet --no-address --tags=allow-glb-health-checks --image-family=debian-11 --image-project=debian-cloud --boot-disk-size=10GB --metadata=startup-script="#! /bin/bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y apache2
echo '<h1>Welcome to Primary Region: US-CENTRAL</h1>' | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html" --project=$MY_PROJ

# 4. Provision the zero-external-IP instance template for the Failover Region (US East)
gcloud compute instance-templates create east-app-template --network=enterprise-global-vpc --subnet=prod-east-app-subnet --no-address --tags=allow-glb-health-checks --image-family=debian-11 --image-project=debian-cloud --boot-disk-size=10GB --metadata=startup-script="#! /bin/bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y apache2
echo '<h1>Welcome to Failover Region: US-EAST</h1>' | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html" --project=$MY_PROJ

# 5. Initialize the multi-zone Managed Instance Group (MIG) container fleet for US Central
gcloud compute instance-groups managed create central-mig --template=central-app-template --size=2 --zones=us-central1-a,us-central1-b --health-check=regional-http-health-check --project=$MY_PROJ

# 6. Initialize the multi-zone Managed Instance Group (MIG) container fleet for US East
gcloud compute instance-groups managed create east-mig --template=east-app-template --size=2 --zones=us-east4-a,us-east4-b --health-check=regional-http-health-check --project=$MY_PROJ
